From 9bd7cd50d533598a9ed99b5538e39e5d016e4696 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sixtyeightk <sixtyeightk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:24:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/18] E4+E7: Switch platform glue (sdmc base dir, no picker,
 applet pause, audio reopen)

runner/platform_switch.{c,h} (empty unless GENESIS_PLATFORM_SWITCH, i.e.
__SWITCH__ or GENESIS_SWITCH_STUBS):

E4
- genesis_switch_base_dir(): sdmc:/switch/<GENESIS_SWITCH_APP_DIR>/, created on
  first use. init_exe_dir() uses it instead of the exe directory and chdirs
  there, so settings.ini, saves, states and runtime evidence land on the SD
  card. Stub builds map sdmc:/ to $GENESIS_FAKE_SDMC (default ./fake-sdmc).
- On the console stderr goes to <base>/log.txt (line-buffered).
- No popen ROM picker on Switch (the ROM is embedded or given as argv[1]).
- runtime_evidence: no module-path lookup on Switch (compile stamp instead).
  The TCP debug server is turned off by the game build (GEN_ENABLE_TRACE=OFF).

E7
- genesis_switch_init() hooks applet focus/resume messages.
- genesis_switch_frame(), once per frame after SDL events: while the app is
  out of focus it pauses (audio off, events and appletMainLoop pumped, 10 ms
  sleeps) and pushes SDL_QUIT if the system asks to exit; when focus returns
  (or after the system resumed a suspended process) it reopens the SDL audio
  device via the new audio_reopen(), since audren output can stay silent
  after a suspension.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
